1
00:00:00,333 --> 00:00:02,350
September nineteen sixty-one.

2
00:00:02,350 --> 00:00:04,993
A dark mountain road in New Hampshire.

3
00:00:04,993 --> 00:00:07,567
A couple in an old car, heading home.

4
00:00:07,567 --> 00:00:10,766
And above them, a light that will not go away.

5
00:00:11,233 --> 00:00:12,736
They arrive hours late.

6
00:00:12,736 --> 00:00:15,089
They cannot say where the time went.

7
00:00:15,089 --> 00:00:19,600
Their dress is torn, their watches have stopped, and they are afraid.

8
00:00:20,066 --> 00:00:26,392
Three years later, in a doctor's office, under hypnosis, the woman draws a map of the stars.

9
00:00:26,392 --> 00:00:32,100
A teacher later says it points to a real star system, thirty-nine light years away.

10
00:00:32,566 --> 00:00:34,485
Tonight, we play the tapes.

11
00:00:34,485 --> 00:00:35,337
Seven reels.

12
00:00:35,337 --> 00:00:37,611
Each one is a piece of the case.

13
00:00:37,611 --> 00:00:40,666
Each one gets a score, evidence, or theory.

14
00:00:41,133 --> 00:00:47,848
This is the story of Betty and Barney Hill, the first famous alien abduction in the world.

15
00:00:47,848 --> 00:00:48,520
Reel one.

16
00:00:48,520 --> 00:00:49,266
The drive.

17
00:00:53,733 --> 00:00:54,345
Reel one.

18
00:00:54,345 --> 00:00:55,025
The drive.

19
00:00:55,025 --> 00:00:58,834
Betty and Barney Hill live in Portsmouth, New Hampshire.

20
00:00:58,834 --> 00:01:00,534
Betty is a social worker.

21
00:01:00,534 --> 00:01:05,772
Barney works for the post office, and is active in the civil rights movement.

22
00:01:05,772 --> 00:01:10,533
In nineteen sixty-one, a mixed-race marriage is still rare, and risky.

23
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:14,997
They take a short holiday, to Niagara Falls and Montreal.

24
00:01:14,997 --> 00:01:23,062
On the night of September nineteenth, they start the long drive home down Route Three, through the White Mountains.

25
00:01:23,062 --> 00:01:25,166
It is late, the road is empty.

26
00:01:25,633 --> 00:01:29,898
Near Lancaster, Betty notices a bright light near the moon.

27
00:01:29,898 --> 00:01:32,789
She thinks it is a star, or a satellite.

28
00:01:32,789 --> 00:01:38,500
But it seems to follow them, growing as the road bends through Franconia Notch.

29
00:01:38,966 --> 00:01:44,161
Near a place called Indian Head, Barney stops and takes out his binoculars.

30
00:01:44,161 --> 00:01:47,694
He sees something crossing the road toward a field.

31
00:01:47,694 --> 00:01:52,266
In his account, a row of windows, and figures looking back at him.

32
00:01:52,733 --> 00:01:57,457
He runs back to the car and shouts that they are about to be captured.

33
00:01:57,457 --> 00:01:59,211
He floors the accelerator.

34
00:01:59,211 --> 00:02:03,733
Then, Betty says, there was a strange buzzing, and a drowsy tingle.

35
00:02:04,200 --> 00:02:05,576
And then a road sign.

36
00:02:05,576 --> 00:02:09,575
They are about thirty-five miles further south, near Ashland.

37
00:02:09,575 --> 00:02:11,673
They do not remember driving it.

38
00:02:11,673 --> 00:02:14,033
This is the first thing on the tape.

39
00:02:14,500 --> 00:02:15,080
Reel two.

40
00:02:15,080 --> 00:02:16,241
The missing miles.

41
00:02:16,241 --> 00:02:19,079
The trip should have taken about four hours.

42
00:02:19,079 --> 00:02:25,400
They get home to Portsmouth around five in the morning, nearly two hours later than they expected.

43
00:02:25,866 --> 00:02:28,354
Betty's dress is torn, and stained.

44
00:02:28,354 --> 00:02:33,044
Barney's shoes are scuffed, the strap of his binoculars is broken.

45
00:02:33,044 --> 00:02:36,811
And the trunk of the car shows strange shiny circles.

46
00:02:36,811 --> 00:02:40,933
Betty's sister later says a compass needle spun near them.

47
00:02:41,400 --> 00:02:43,528
So how much of the gap is real?

48
00:02:43,528 --> 00:02:48,882
The two hours are estimated from memory, since neither of them noted the time.

49
00:02:48,882 --> 00:02:56,433
But investigators later made one odd point: the moon, which they thought was the strange orb, had already set.

50
00:02:56,900 --> 00:03:03,386
The next day, Betty picks up the phone and calls Pease Air Force Base, a few miles from home.

51
00:03:03,386 --> 00:03:09,733
An officer takes their story, and a report is sent on to the Air Force's Project Blue Book.

52
00:03:10,199 --> 00:03:11,458
Notice the order.

53
00:03:11,458 --> 00:03:17,086
This report was filed before any hypnosis, before any book, before any fame.

54
00:03:17,086 --> 00:03:20,345
It is the oldest solid evidence in the case.

55
00:03:20,345 --> 00:03:23,233
A real couple, reporting a real fright.

56
00:03:23,699 --> 00:03:28,100
In October, a civilian group called NICAP sends investigators.

57
00:03:28,100 --> 00:03:30,656
They interview the couple for hours.

58
00:03:30,656 --> 00:03:34,063
They find them sincere, intelligent, and shaken.

59
00:03:34,063 --> 00:03:35,766
They do not find a hoax.

60
00:03:36,233 --> 00:03:38,219
But Barney is not sleeping.

61
00:03:38,219 --> 00:03:39,763
He has stomach pains.

62
00:03:39,763 --> 00:03:41,602
His blood pressure rises.

63
00:03:41,602 --> 00:03:43,661
His doctor sees real stress.

64
00:03:43,661 --> 00:03:47,633
Betty tells a friend she keeps having terrible dreams.

65
00:03:48,099 --> 00:03:56,196
Honest question: is a long drive at night, a bright planet, and a fright enough to explain a gap of two hours?

66
00:03:56,196 --> 00:03:57,447
Skeptics say yes.

67
00:03:57,447 --> 00:03:58,698
Believers say no.

68
00:03:58,698 --> 00:04:00,833
The tape alone cannot decide.

69
00:04:01,300 --> 00:04:06,826
Some skeptics point out that Jupiter and Saturn were both very bright that month.

70
00:04:06,826 --> 00:04:07,167
Fine.

71
00:04:07,167 --> 00:04:12,966
But Jupiter does not cross a highway, and it does not explain two hours of lost time.

72
00:04:13,433 --> 00:04:18,985
So at the end of reel two we have a frightened couple, a strange sighting, and a gap.

73
00:04:18,985 --> 00:04:21,402
Next, the part that made them famous.

74
00:04:21,402 --> 00:04:23,166
The dreams, and the doctor.

75
00:04:23,633 --> 00:04:24,359
Reel three.

76
00:04:24,359 --> 00:04:26,140
The dreams, and the doctor.

77
00:04:26,140 --> 00:04:30,362
In the weeks after the drive, Betty dreams of the missing night.

78
00:04:30,362 --> 00:04:36,366
She dreams of men stopping the car, and walking them into the woods, toward a bright craft.

79
00:04:36,833 --> 00:04:38,774
She writes the dreams down.

80
00:04:38,774 --> 00:04:45,243
She also reads about flying saucers, and writes to a well-known UFO author, Donald Keyhoe.

81
00:04:45,243 --> 00:04:47,400
That detail will matter later.

82
00:04:47,866 --> 00:05:00,833
Barney's troubles lead to a psychiatrist, and then to a Boston specialist: Doctor Benjamin Simon, who spent the Second World War treating soldiers with memory loss, using hypnosis.

83
00:05:01,300 --> 00:05:07,273
From January to June nineteen sixty-four, the Hills visit his office, again and again.

84
00:05:07,273 --> 00:05:12,205
He hypnotizes them separately, so that neither can influence the other.

85
00:05:12,205 --> 00:05:14,566
Every session is recorded on tape.

86
00:05:15,033 --> 00:05:16,978
Those recordings still exist.

87
00:05:16,978 --> 00:05:21,136
The story that comes out of them is the story the world knows.

88
00:05:21,136 --> 00:05:26,166
It begins on a dark road, with a group of men standing in front of the car.

89
00:05:26,633 --> 00:05:30,674
Under hypnosis, Betty describes being led to a craft.

90
00:05:30,674 --> 00:05:33,190
Inside, small beings examine her.

91
00:05:33,190 --> 00:05:35,553
They take hair, skin and nails.

92
00:05:35,553 --> 00:05:37,764
A needle goes into her navel.

93
00:05:37,764 --> 00:05:40,433
She is told it is a pregnancy test.

94
00:05:40,899 --> 00:05:43,961
Barney's account is shorter and more frightened.

95
00:05:43,961 --> 00:05:47,979
He remembers his eyes shut tight, and a cup placed against him.

96
00:05:47,979 --> 00:05:53,399
He tells the doctor the beings had eyes that wrapped around the sides of their heads.

97
00:05:53,866 --> 00:05:56,054
What did Doctor Simon make of it?

98
00:05:56,054 --> 00:05:58,707
He believed that the Hills were sincere.

99
00:05:58,707 --> 00:06:01,757
But he did not believe in a literal abduction.

100
00:06:01,757 --> 00:06:06,266
He thought it was a powerful fantasy that began with Betty's dreams.

101
00:06:06,733 --> 00:06:13,178
And then, near the end of the sessions, comes the moment that turned a local story into a legend.

102
00:06:13,178 --> 00:06:16,699
Betty is asked to draw something she saw on the ship.

103
00:06:17,166 --> 00:06:17,865
Reel four.

104
00:06:17,865 --> 00:06:18,773
The star map.

105
00:06:18,773 --> 00:06:22,268
Betty says she saw a map on the wall of the craft.

106
00:06:22,268 --> 00:06:26,670
A leader showed it to her, when she asked where they came from.

107
00:06:26,670 --> 00:06:30,933
She draws it from memory: a handful of dots, joined by lines.

108
00:06:31,399 --> 00:06:36,699
Four years later, a schoolteacher in Ohio reads the book about the case.

109
00:06:36,699 --> 00:06:39,569
Marjorie Fish is an amateur astronomer.

110
00:06:39,569 --> 00:06:42,146
She wonders: could the map be real?

111
00:06:42,146 --> 00:06:44,133
Could she find those stars?

112
00:06:44,600 --> 00:06:47,731
The library will not lend its star catalogues.

113
00:06:47,731 --> 00:06:57,533
So she copies the positions of more than a thousand nearby stars, by hand, and turns them into a three-dimensional model, with beads on strings.

114
00:06:58,000 --> 00:06:58,922
She turns it.

115
00:06:58,922 --> 00:07:00,058
She tries again.

116
00:07:00,058 --> 00:07:04,602
After years, she says she finds a view where the pattern clicks.

117
00:07:04,602 --> 00:07:11,133
A double star in the southern sky, called Zeta Reticuli, about thirty-nine light years away.

118
00:07:11,600 --> 00:07:16,978
In the mid nineteen seventies, a leading astronomy magazine publishes her work.

119
00:07:16,978 --> 00:07:19,973
Suddenly the case is not just a ghost story.

120
00:07:19,973 --> 00:07:22,833
It looks like a prediction that came true.

121
00:07:23,300 --> 00:07:25,118
Other astronomers push back.

122
00:07:25,118 --> 00:07:29,663
With a thousand stars to choose from, you can find a pattern anywhere.

123
00:07:29,663 --> 00:07:34,533
Fish chose which stars to link, and which to skip, after seeing the sketch.

124
00:07:35,000 --> 00:07:38,780
Newer measurements also shift some of those stars.

125
00:07:38,780 --> 00:07:41,881
The neat pattern no longer holds up well.

126
00:07:41,881 --> 00:07:45,284
Zeta Reticuli is real, and it is a fine star.

127
00:07:45,284 --> 00:07:48,233
But it is an interpretation, not proof.

128
00:07:48,699 --> 00:07:49,441
Reel five.

129
00:07:49,441 --> 00:07:51,073
The hypnosis question.

130
00:07:51,073 --> 00:07:54,931
Everything dramatic in the case comes from hypnosis.

131
00:07:54,931 --> 00:07:58,566
So how good is hypnosis at finding true memories?

132
00:07:59,033 --> 00:08:03,893
Researchers have studied this for decades, and the answer is not kind.

133
00:08:03,893 --> 00:08:07,156
Hypnosis can make you feel sure about a memory.

134
00:08:07,156 --> 00:08:10,072
It does not make the memory more accurate.

135
00:08:10,072 --> 00:08:11,600
It can plant new ones.

136
00:08:12,066 --> 00:08:13,746
Memory itself is fragile.

137
00:08:13,746 --> 00:08:15,560
Each retelling reshapes it.

138
00:08:15,560 --> 00:08:22,481
And in this case, the Hills had lived with the story for more than two years before the sessions began.

139
00:08:22,481 --> 00:08:24,833
They had talked it over many times.

140
00:08:25,300 --> 00:08:28,553
There is also what the culture was feeding them.

141
00:08:28,553 --> 00:08:33,230
In the early sixties, flying saucers were on television and in books.

142
00:08:33,230 --> 00:08:37,500
A frightened mind can build a story from anything it has heard.

143
00:08:37,966 --> 00:08:40,052
But here is the fairness test.

144
00:08:40,052 --> 00:08:43,667
The Hills told the story only to small local groups.

145
00:08:43,667 --> 00:08:50,133
When a newspaper learned of it, in October nineteen sixty-five, they asked for it not to run.

146
00:08:50,600 --> 00:08:56,798
Five days of headlines followed, and a bestselling book by John Fuller, The Interrupted Journey.

147
00:08:56,798 --> 00:09:00,608
Honest people, then, who really believed in what they said.

148
00:09:00,608 --> 00:09:02,933
Belief is not proof, but it matters.

149
00:09:03,399 --> 00:09:09,937
So the hypnosis tapes are real documents of what the Hills believed in nineteen sixty-four.

150
00:09:09,937 --> 00:09:14,463
They are not a window onto what happened in nineteen sixty-one.

151
00:09:14,463 --> 00:09:15,899
One more reel to go.

152
00:09:16,366 --> 00:09:17,011
Reel six.

153
00:09:17,011 --> 00:09:18,373
The skeptic's file.

154
00:09:18,373 --> 00:09:29,700
In February nineteen sixty-four, weeks into the sessions, a television drama called The Outer Limits aired an episode featuring an alien with wraparound eyes.

155
00:09:30,166 --> 00:09:34,710
Barney's later description of the beings' eyes has the same shape.

156
00:09:34,710 --> 00:09:38,221
That is the sharpest coincidence skeptics point to.

157
00:09:38,221 --> 00:09:43,866
But Betty said she had described similar eyes in her dreams of nineteen sixty-one.

158
00:09:44,333 --> 00:09:46,906
And the pair did not match perfectly.

159
00:09:46,906 --> 00:09:50,383
Barney recalled the aliens one way, Betty another.

160
00:09:50,383 --> 00:09:55,738
Doctor Simon thought Barney's version looked absorbed from his wife's dreams.

161
00:09:55,738 --> 00:09:58,033
Skeptics call that contamination.

162
00:09:58,500 --> 00:10:03,442
Writers like Philip Klass and Robert Sheaffer also dug through the files.

163
00:10:03,442 --> 00:10:08,723
They pointed to the bright planets, to hypnosis, and to a mind already primed.

164
00:10:08,723 --> 00:10:11,500
They argued it was a vivid dream, shared.

165
00:10:11,966 --> 00:10:14,464
There are other human explanations.

166
00:10:14,464 --> 00:10:18,817
Sleep paralysis, which brings visions of figures in the room.

167
00:10:18,817 --> 00:10:22,171
Highway hypnosis, after hours of night driving.

168
00:10:22,171 --> 00:10:27,166
Stress, in a mixed-race couple on a lonely road in nineteen sixty-one.

169
00:10:27,633 --> 00:10:31,496
None of these can be tested, so the verdict stays open.

170
00:10:31,496 --> 00:10:35,709
But notice: no one has found a hoax, no lie, no paid script.

171
00:10:35,709 --> 00:10:38,799
That is why the case still unsettles people.

172
00:10:39,266 --> 00:10:40,219
One reel left.

173
00:10:40,219 --> 00:10:49,066
It follows the Hills after the tapes stop, and what happens when a private fright becomes the world's first alien abduction story.

174
00:10:49,533 --> 00:10:50,333
Reel seven.

175
00:10:50,333 --> 00:10:51,496
After the tapes.

176
00:10:51,496 --> 00:10:55,568
The Interrupted Journey comes out in nineteen sixty-six.

177
00:10:55,568 --> 00:10:57,531
A magazine prints extracts.

178
00:10:57,531 --> 00:11:04,366
It sells in the millions, and it sets the template: grey beings, a medical exam, missing time.

179
00:11:04,833 --> 00:11:13,358
In nineteen seventy-five, NBC turns it into a television film, The UFO Incident, with James Earl Jones as Barney.

180
00:11:13,358 --> 00:11:14,490
Millions watch.

181
00:11:14,490 --> 00:11:21,733
In the years that follow, abduction reports multiply, and they look more and more like this one.

182
00:11:22,200 --> 00:11:24,383
Barney does not live to see it.

183
00:11:24,383 --> 00:11:28,540
He dies of a stroke in nineteen sixty-nine, aged forty-six.

184
00:11:28,540 --> 00:11:29,738
Betty carries on.

185
00:11:29,738 --> 00:11:38,333
She gives talks, writes to researchers, and keeps saying she sees lights in the sky, until her death in two thousand four.

186
00:11:38,799 --> 00:11:46,159
Today the Hills' papers, tapes, and that blue dress rest in the archive at the University of New Hampshire.

187
00:11:46,159 --> 00:11:49,666
A real, quiet collection of an extraordinary story.

188
00:11:50,133 --> 00:11:52,170
Here is the strangest result.

189
00:11:52,170 --> 00:11:56,035
A couple who never wanted fame gave the world a script.

190
00:11:56,035 --> 00:11:58,845
Grey beings, bright craft, missing time.

191
00:11:58,845 --> 00:12:01,866
Whether true or not, it entered our dreams.

192
00:12:02,333 --> 00:12:03,319
Now, the court.

193
00:12:03,319 --> 00:12:05,816
Seven reels, seven pieces of evidence.

194
00:12:05,816 --> 00:12:06,933
Let's score them.

195
00:12:07,399 --> 00:12:07,912
Debrief.

196
00:12:07,912 --> 00:12:09,258
The tapes are played.

197
00:12:09,258 --> 00:12:10,733
Time for the scorecard.

198
00:12:11,200 --> 00:12:11,703
Debrief.

199
00:12:11,703 --> 00:12:13,466
Time to score the Hill case.

200
00:12:13,933 --> 00:12:19,875
A real couple, a real drive, and a real fright on September nineteenth: evidence.

201
00:12:19,875 --> 00:12:24,717
A report to the Air Force within a day, before hypnosis: evidence.

202
00:12:24,717 --> 00:12:30,000
Two hours missing: partial, because it rests on memory and rough timing.

203
00:12:30,466 --> 00:12:34,942
Torn dress, shiny marks, stopped watches: unverified.

204
00:12:34,942 --> 00:12:38,996
Hypnosis memories as fact: debunked as a method.

205
00:12:38,996 --> 00:12:42,206
The Zeta Reticuli star map: contested.

206
00:12:42,206 --> 00:12:45,500
A literal alien abduction: no evidence.

207
00:12:45,966 --> 00:12:46,768
The verdict.

208
00:12:46,768 --> 00:12:48,106
Sincere, not proven.

209
00:12:48,106 --> 00:12:53,922
Betty and Barney Hill most likely told the truth about their fear, and about the light.

210
00:12:53,922 --> 00:12:57,799
But what happened in those two hours, no tape can tell us.

211
00:12:58,266 --> 00:13:01,068
Maybe it was a dream, shared and shaped.

212
00:13:01,068 --> 00:13:03,869
Maybe a mystery we still cannot explain.

213
00:13:03,869 --> 00:13:05,760
What it was not, is a hoax.

214
00:13:05,760 --> 00:13:10,033
And that is why, sixty years on, the tapes are still playing.

215
00:13:10,500 --> 00:13:21,500
Next case: a policeman chasing a speeding car on a New Mexico road in nineteen sixty-four hears a roar, sees a flash, and walks toward an egg-shaped craft.

216
00:13:21,500 --> 00:13:23,700
And leaves burned brush behind.

217
00:13:24,166 --> 00:13:26,586
What do you think happened on that road?

218
00:13:26,586 --> 00:13:31,666
Tell us in the comments, and subscribe for the next ancient mystery put to the test.
